class:: Vlive
summary:: Pbind that produces persistent live-input visual events
categories:: Libraries>VisualServer
related:: Classes/Vbind, Classes/LiveParam, Classes/VisualSynthDef, Guides/VisualServer, Reference/VisualParameters

description::

Factory returning a link::Classes/Pbind:: pre-seeded with code::(type: \vlive, dur: inf, view: \default)::. Targets the code::\live:: link::Classes/VisualSynthDef::. Because code::dur:: defaults to code::inf::, nodes are strong::persistent:: (never auto-freed) and their function-valued params are evaluated every frame — ideal for sensor/data-driven visuals. See link::Classes/Vbind:: for the playback model and link::Classes/LiveParam:: for streaming a value per event.

CLASSMETHODS::

method:: new
argument:: ... pairs
Common keys: code::x y size color fill view::. Values are typically link::Classes/Function::s.
returns:: a link::Classes/Pbind::.

EXAMPLES::

code::
~imu = (x: 0, y: 0);
Routine({ loop { ~imu.x = sin(thisThread.seconds); ~imu.y = cos(thisThread.seconds); 0.05.wait } }).play;

Vlive(\x, { ~imu.x }, \y, { ~imu.y }, \size, 60,
    \color, { Color.hsv(~imu.x.abs, 0.8, 1) }, \view, \demo).vplay;
::
